{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal model using scvi_n200 RNA encoding and ViT (imagenet_vit_l) image encoding with concat fusion, replacing resnet50 in previous multimodal configurations. Validation accuracy of 0.532 is lower than RNA-only multiprofile baselines (0.65) but slightly higher than RNA-only singleprofile models (0.520). The result suggests ViT may not improve performance compared to resnet50 in this setup, though uncertainty remains due to differing profile settings and untested aggregation/fusion interactions."
}

